"b8083c0d-bf14-4263-a25e-39e1da61bc2d"]},"b8083c0d-bf14-4263-a25e-39e1da61bc2d":{"id":"b8083c0d-bf14-4263-a25e-39e1da61bc2d","message":{"id":"b8083c0d-bf14-4263-a25e-39e1da61bc2d","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{"real_author":"tool:web"}},"create_time":1732978521.1610832,"update_time":null,"content":{"content_type":"text","parts":["To enhance storage performance on Windows 10 by combining two drives into a single striped volume (RAID 0), follow these steps:\n\n**Important Considerations:**\n\n- **Data Loss Warning:** Creating a striped volume will erase all data on the selected drives. Ensure you back up any important data before proceeding.\n- **Drive Compatibility:** For optimal performance, use drives of identical size and speed.\n- **Lack of Redundancy:** RAID 0 offers no fault tolerance; if one drive fails, all data in the array is lost. Regular backups are essential.\n\n**Steps to Create a Striped Volume:**\n\n1. **Open Disk Management:**\n   - Press `Win + X` and select **Disk Management** from the menu.\n\n2. **Delete Existing Volumes:**\n   - In Disk Management, right-click each volume on the drives you want to combine and select **Delete Volume**. Confirm the deletion. This action will convert the space to \"Unallocated.\"\n\n3. **Initiate New Striped Volume:**\n   - Right-click on the unallocated space of one of the drives and choose **New Striped Volume**.\n\n4. **Add Drives to the Striped Volume:**\n   - The New Striped Volume Wizard will open. Click **Next**, select the additional drive(s) to include in the striped volume, and click **Add**.\n\n5. **Assign Drive Letter or Path:**\n   - Choose a drive letter or mount the volume in an empty NTFS folder. Click **Next**.\n\n6. **Format the Volume:**\n   - Set the file system to **NTFS**, allocation unit size to **Default**, and provide a volume label. Check the **Perform a quick format** option. Click **Next**.\n\n7. **Complete the Setup:**\n   - Review your settings and click **Finish**. You'll be prompted to convert the selected disks to dynamic disks; click **Yes** to proceed.\n\nAfter completing these steps, Windows will format the new striped volume, and it will appear as a single drive in File Explorer.\n\n**Additional Resources:**\n\n- **Video Tutorial:** For a visual guide, you can watch the following video:\n\nvideoCreate a Striped Volume (RAID 0) With Multiple Disks in Windowsturn0search1\n\n- **Detailed Guide:** For more information, refer to this comprehensive article: citeturn0search0\n\n**Disclaimer:** Proceed with caution when modifying disk configurations. Ensure all important data is backed up, and understand the implications of using RAID 0, including the increased risk of data loss due to lack of redundancy. "]},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"weight":1,"metadata":{"search_source":"composer_auto","client_reported_search_source":"composer_auto","search_result_groups":[{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"windowscentral.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.windowscentral.com/how-create-one-large-volume-using-multiple-hard-drives-windows-10","title":"How to combine multiple hard drives into one volume on Windows 10","snippet":"When you have multiple hard drives on your computer, it can quickly become hard to keep track where your files are located. However, similar to previous versions, Windows 10 includes two features ...","ref_id":{"turn_index":0,"ref_type":"search","ref_index":0},"content_type":null,"pub_date":1464739200,"attributions":null,"attributions_debug":null}]},{"type":"search_result_group","domain":"youtube.com","entries":[{"type":"search_result","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3-v-BGDJvDE","title":"Create a Striped Volume (RAID 0) With Multiple Disks in Windows","snippet":"Windows will let you take multiple hard drives and combine them into a single striped volume (also known as RAID 0) so you can utilize all of the disks with ...",